// ONE-TIME MIGRATION DATA -- do not edit, do not regenerate.
//
//   - This is a frozen snapshot of what each practice entry's
//     content-derived id (see js/id-utils.js) was, indexed by its
//     POSITION in data/practices.js at the moment this project
//     moved from positional ids (practice-${i}) to content-derived
//     ids.
//   - It exists for exactly one purpose: js/practice-mastery.js
//     uses it once, at boot, to translate any
//     practice-mastery:practice-<N> key left over in a learner's
//     localStorage from before this migration into the matching
//     practice-mastery:<contentId> key, so previously earned
//     "Mastered" progress survives the switch. Once an old key is
//     migrated it is deleted, so this table only ever does real
//     work once per browser.
//   - This array is intentionally static and must NOT be
//     regenerated from the current data/practices.js -- its whole
//     value is that it reflects the OLD file layout that the old
//     positional ids were computed against. Edits to
//     data/practices.js after this migration (reordering, adding,
//     removing entries) do not touch this file and do not need to.
//   - Two old positions may map to the same id: that happened
//     naturally where the old dataset had a true duplicate
//     question (identical content hashes to the same id), and the
//     migration correctly merges their mastered state onto the one
//     surviving card instead of losing either learner's progress.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

